---
title: Moroccan Whole Boiled-Orange and Almond Cake
servings: 6
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Moroccan
---

Place two whole @oranges{2%large}(unwaxed and unpeeled) in a #saucepan{}, cover completely with water, bring to a boil, and simmer gently with a lid on for 1½ to ~{2%hours} until they are very soft. Drain and let them cool completely.

Preheat the oven to 150°C and line a #23 cm (9") springform or round cake tin{} with baking paper.

Cut the cooled oranges in half and remove any seeds. Place the entire oranges (peel, pith, and pulp) into a food processor and blitz until it forms a smooth purée. Add the @eggs{6%large}, @caster sugar{250%g}, @ground almonds{250%g}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, and optional @?ground cardamon{0.5%tsp} and/or @?orange blossom water{1%tsp}. Pulse/blitz for 15 to ~{20%seconds} until completely smooth and combined. Scrape down the sides once, pulse for another ~{5%seconds}, and pour straight into the lined cake tin.

Bake for ~{1%hour}. Check at 45 minutes; if the top is browning too quickly, cover it loosely with a sheet of foil. The cake is done when a skewer inserted into the center comes out clean and the top feels firm to a light touch.

Allow to cool in the tin before turning out.